{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Moses took his wife and his sons.</b> Because the sons were small and still needed their mother, he seated the mother first and afterward the children in her lap. But regarding Jacob, whose sons were grown, it writes his sons first and afterward his wives." "<b>And he returned to the land of Egypt.</b> He alone, for as soon as HaShem met Moses, Eliezer was circumcised, and Moses left them there and Moses went from there to Egypt; and when Eliezer recovered from his circumcision, Zipporah and her two sons returned to her father." "<b>The staff of HaShem.</b> It is not yet called by the name of Moses, because up to that time he had not performed a sign with it."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:09.061914975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}